{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHtgnM7GjuXo46Z7i1tx8d","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart\",\"number\":3793,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(fix) O3-6097: Fix inverted labels on the free text dosage toggle\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"sudeshkar\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-12T15:51:32.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-12T17:54:09.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-10-12T17:54:09.000Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/pull/3793\",\"mergeCommit\":\"1c19126f11ca5bb93891bd18d89910d20f41ee84\",\"syncedAt\":\"2026-10-24T04:03:34.106Z\",\"tickets\":[{\"key\":\"O3-6097\",\"source\":\"ticket-pattern\"}],\"commits\":[{\"sha\":\"1c19126f11ca5bb93891bd18d89910d20f41ee84\",\"source\":\"merge-commit-sha\",\"verified\":true}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"packages/esm-patient-medications-app/src/add-drug-order/drug-order-form.component.tsx\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":2},{\"path\":\"packages/esm-patient-medications-app/src/add-drug-order/drug-order-form.test.tsx\",\"additions\":16,\"deletions\":0}],\"body\":\"## Requirements\\n\\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe \\\"Free text dosage\\\" toggle in the drug order form was showing the opposite of its actual state. It read \\\"On\\\" while switched off (structured Dose / Route / Frequency fields showing) and \\\"Off\\\" once switched on (free-text box showing). The same thing happened in other languages, e.g. French showed \\\"Activé\\\" while the toggle was off.\\n\\nThis could lead a clinician to believe structured dosing was selected while they were actually typing into the free-text box, which is how orders with no dose, route, frequency or duration were ending up saved and stuck in Active Medications.\\n\\nThe cause was the labels passed to Carbon's `Toggle` in `drug-order-form.component.tsx`. Carbon shows `labelA` when unchecked and `labelB` when checked, and we had them the other way round. I swapped them so the label now matches the toggle state, and added a test that checks the label text in both states. No translation changes are needed since the `on` / `off` keys already exist.\\n\\n## Screenshots\\n\\nFree text dosage switched on, label now reads \\\"On\\\":\\n\\n<img width=\\\"636\\\" height=\\\"972\\\" alt=\\\"Fix\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a6090c8-7d65-4804-8c11-c9dacac6cc2a\\\" />\\n\\n## Related Issue\\n\\nhttps://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3-6097\\n\\n## Other\\n\\nN/A\\n\",\"freshness\":[{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart\",\"lastSyncedAt\":\"2026-10-24T04:03:34.106Z\",\"stale\":false}],\"nextOffset\":null,\"truncated\":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cd84b84-9b20-4e2b-a4eb-7540069dbf26","uuid":"ba75b783-91ef-43e6-b7a3-823d7078948b","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:26:44.901Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart\",\"number\":3793,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(fix) O3-6097: Fix inverted labels on the free text dosage toggle\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"sudeshkar\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-12T15:51:32.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-12T17:54:09.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-10-12T17:54:09.000Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/pull/3793\",\"mergeCommit\":\"1c19126f11ca5bb93891bd18d89910d20f41ee84\",\"syncedAt\":\"2026-10-24T04:03:34.106Z\",\"tickets\":[{\"key\":\"O3-6097